# First-shift vista beat (council memo docs/council/2026-07-16-design-magnetism.md, item 5): one
# private PROVIDENCE line per map, delivered once per player per round when a player with an active
# First Shift assignment first walks past that map's composed-vista marker (SolreignVistaBeatSystem,
# solreign.first_shift_vista_beat). House corporate-sinister-warm voice, PG-13. Every visual each
# line references was grep-verified present at the marker's spot in that map's file (see
# docs/receipts/VISTA-BEAT-2026-07-17.md for the per-map evidence table) — these lines must never be
# reused across maps.

## Leviathan — cargo/QM corridor outside the quartermaster's office window: a bioluminescent potted
## plant and a gold desk lamp glow behind the glass, and raw asteroid rock breaches the corridor a
## few tiles on.

solreign-vista-leviathan = A moment, asset. Behind the quartermaster's glass, a plant glows without being asked to. A little further on, the asteroid is still coming through the wall. Solreign retains both, and notes which one you stopped for.

## Meridian — the arrivals-side corridor: a run of reinforced windows onto open space to one side,
## the executive lounge (gold lamp, comfy chairs, a Cohiba Robusto cigar ad) behind interior glass
## on the other.

solreign-vista-meridian = Observe the glass, asset. On one side, the void — vast, and off the books. On the other, the lounge: a gold lamp, soft chairs, a cigar advertisement. Solreign finds it clarifying that you can see both from where you stand.

## Nocturne — the dim blue-carpet promenade from arrivals: low light by design, two waiting chairs
## against the wall beneath a "Just a Week Away..." poster.

solreign-vista-nocturne = Solreign keeps the lights low here, asset. The blue carpet knows the way. The poster above the waiting chairs says it is just a week away. It has said so for as long as we have measured.

## Oasis — the loading dock outside the quartermaster's glass door: a wall-mounted carp and a map
## of Saltern Station hang in the office beyond.

solreign-vista-oasis = Note the quartermaster's office, asset: a fish mounted on the wall, and a map of a different station entirely. Trophies and elsewheres. Solreign encourages you to earn the first before considering the second.

## Perihelion — the cargo bay beside the First Shift beacon: through the QM office's interior glass,
## a lit fireplace, black carpet, and a gold cigar on the desk.

solreign-vista-perihelion = Through the office glass, asset: a fireplace, lit, on company time. Warmth at that grade is earned, not issued. Solreign invites you to appreciate it from your side of the window.

## Terminus — the contracts hall: the contracts board, a personal support cube, and the locked
## employee reward cake display, all within a few steps.

solreign-vista-terminus = Here, asset: the contracts board, a personal support cube, and the employee reward cake display. Everything you may one day be awarded, arranged at eye level. Newcomers walk slower here. Solreign understands.

## Verdant — the cargo bay corner where corporate kudzu climbs the crates and an acid-green
## photosynthesis compliance unit lights them.

solreign-vista-verdant = See the kudzu on the crates, asset, and the unit that lights it acid-green. Growth is encouraged at Solreign. Containment is scheduled. Both are further along than they appear.
